[b]v0.2.0:[/b]
[h1]Flavorium Universalis — v0.2 Update[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.2.* | Multiplayer synchronized | Save-game compatible[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]New: Dynamic AI Personalities[/h2]

AI countries now evolve their strategic behavior across the ages rather than holding the same personality from start to finish.

[b]27 countries[/b] have historically-grounded personality arcs: TUR, FRA, ENG, MOS, CAS, HAB, POR, SWE, POL, LIT, DAN, BUR, VEN, PAP, GEN, BYZ, HUN, MAM, ETH, MNG, SHO, KOR, NOG/GLH, NAP, SCO, MLO, MLI, SON

[b]Historical inflection events[/b] fire at key turning points and give player-controlled countries a choice:
[list]
[*] [b]The Conquering Sultan[/b] (TUR, Age 3) — peak Selim/Suleiman era
[*] [b]The Long Stagnation[/b] (TUR, Age 4) — early Ottoman decline begins
[*] [b]The Sun King Rises[/b] (FRA, Age 5) — Louis XIV's absolutist ambition
[*] [b]Britannia's Maritime Empire[/b] (ENG, Age 5) — English naval and commercial dominance
[*] [b]The Terrible Tsar[/b] (MOS, Age 3) — Ivan the Terrible's consolidation
[*] [b]The New World Empire[/b] (CAS, Age 3) — Castilian colonial apex
[*] [b]The Great Northern Reckoning[/b] (SWE, Age 4) — Swedish imperial overstretch
[/list]

After a historical event fires, an AI personality guard prevents random drift from overriding the assignment for ~20 years.

[b]Game rule — C&C: Dynamic AI Personalities[/b] (4 modes, default: Dynamic Historical + Drift)
[list]
[*] [b]Vanilla[/b] — no changes, vanilla personality rules only
[*] [b]Dynamic Historical[/b] — major powers follow age-based arcs with inflection events
[*] [b]Dynamic Drift Only[/b] — context-driven personality shifts for all AI based on war, wealth, and power
[*] [b]Dynamic Historical + Drift[/b] (default) — both systems active
[/list]

[i]~18 inflection events; drift logic fires on yearly and four-yearly pulses.[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]New: Hundred Years War Flavor[/h2]

A system of historical events and starting modifiers for the Hundred Years War situation.

[list]
[*] [b]France and England[/b] begin with historical starting modifiers reflecting their positions at the opening of the conflict
[*] [b]War outcome stacking[/b] — winning and losing major wars accumulates levy and estate effects over time (cc_hyw.10/11)
[*] [b]Observer power reactions[/b] — Burgundy, Castile, and Aragon watch western European wars and may intervene or demand concessions (cc_hyw.12/13)
[*] [b]Vassal defection pressure[/b] — French and English vassals face events when their suzerain suffers defeat (cc_hyw.20–23)
[*] [b]Lowlands succession events[/b] — Lowlands political crises emerge when Burgundy weakens or the war concludes (cc_hyw.30/31)
[*] [b]The Auld Alliance[/b] (cc_hyw.1) — France can formally guarantee Scottish independence to bind England's northern flank
[*] [b]Replace Appanage Ruler[/b] decision — France can remove a disloyal appanage lord before prosecuting the war
[/list]

[b]Game rule — C&C: France — Hundred Years War Flavor[/b] (default: on)
Disable to remove all HYW-specific starting modifiers, stacking events, and vassal defection pressure.

[i]11 events spanning France, England, Scotland, Burgundy, and observer powers.[/i]

[hr][/hr]

